{"title":"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55ba655aaf217c757469f836cd86041a920fdf18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2002}{m^2 -2}\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>a positive integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2afc9a939102362683108c7bfad66bbdedfb64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) one} \\qquad \\text{(B) two} \\qquad \\text{(C) three} \\qquad \\text{(D) four} \\qquad \\text{(E) more than four}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"513\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac72a63cb54f9eba88e6f40307e6e750feda27a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2002}{m^2 -2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"61\" height=\"40\" /> to be an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e470b7ce7a2f4d0c1ae064d2874ca377693897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31084925fe499300805e8fc38476292fc760120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2-2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> Again, memorizing the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e470b7ce7a2f4d0c1ae064d2874ca377693897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is helpful. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1f7966326df6dd9ba26e4ed6cfc2d81a0182792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2002 = 2 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"156\" height=\"14\" />, so its factors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/1359bc5115fd358839dbeb6e20dc41bb2498cc1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 7, 11, 13, 14, 22, 26, 77, 91, 143, 154, 182, 286, 1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"415\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e470b7ce7a2f4d0c1ae064d2874ca377693897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>From this adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the items in our list and checking if they are perfect squares will suffice. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c916cacabaab9edf2df907e78a0051f7f812c429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> end up being our perfect squares, giving us an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed0ebd9db43b5c849671bb9f5a56732f2a83bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\text{three}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P\">2002 AMC 12P</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Prob